"text": "Soit $B$ la matrice de $\\varphi - 3Id_{\\mathbb{R}^{3}}$\n\n$$B = \\begin{pmatrix}\n0 & 4 & - 4 \\\\\n2 & - 1 & - 1 \\\\\n2 & 3 & - 5\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n$$B\\sim\\begin{pmatrix}\n2 & - 1 & - 1 \\\\\n2 & 3 & - 5 \\\\\n0 & 4 & - 4\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n$$B\\sim\\begin{pmatrix}\n2 & - 1 & - 1 \\\\\n0 & 4 & - 4 \\\\\n0 & 4 & - 4\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n$$B\\sim\\begin{pmatrix}\n2 & - 1 & - 1 \\\\\n0 & 1 & - 1 \\\\\n0 & 0 & 0\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n$$B\\sim\\begin{pmatrix}\n2 & 0 & - 2 \\\\\n0 & 1 & - 1 \\\\\n0 & 0 & 0\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n$$B\\sim\\begin{pmatrix}\n1 & 0 & - 1 \\\\\n0 & 1 & - 1 \\\\\n0 & 0 & 0\n\\end{pmatrix}$$\n\n$$(\\varphi - 3Id)(x,y,z) = 0 \\Longleftrightarrow (x,y,z) = (z,z,z)$$\n\n$$Ker(\\varphi - 3Id) = Vect\\left\\{ (1,1,1) \\right\\}$$"
