"text": "Exercice 10\nSoit In =\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)ndt.\n1. ´Etablir une relation de r´ ecurrence entreIn et In+1.\n2. Calculer In.\n3. En d´ eduire\nn∑_{k=0} (−1)k\n2k + 1\n(nₖ\n)\n.\n1. Utilisons la m´ ethode d’int´ egrations par parties. Pour cela, posons\nu(t) = (1 −t2)n+1\nv(t) = t\nu′(t) = −2(n + 1)t(1−t2)n\nv′(t) = 1\n\nAinsi\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)n+1dt =\n[\nt(1−t2)n+1]1\n0 + 2(n + 1)\n∫ 1\n0\nt2(1−t2)ndt\n= 0 + 2( n + 1)\n∫ 1\n0\n(t2− 1 + 1)(1−t2)ndt\n= 2( n + 1)\n∫ 1\n0\n−(1−t2)n+1 + (1 −t2)ndt.\nD’o` u\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)n+1dt = 2( n + 1)\n∫ 1\n0\n−(1−t2)n+1 + (1 −t2)ndt\n= −2(n + 1)\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)n+1 dt + 2(n + 1)\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)ndt\n= −2(n + 1)In+1 + 2(n + 1)In.\nIn+1 = −2(n + 1)In+1 + 2(n + 1)In =⇒ In+1 = 2n + 2\n2n + 3In.\n2. Calculer In : `A l’aide de l’identit´ e pr´ ec´ edente, nous pouvons ´ ecrire\nIn = 2(n− 1) + 2\n2(n− 1) + 3In−1 = 2n\n2n + 1In−1\n= 2n\n2n + 1· 2n− 2\n2n− 1In−2\n...\n= 2n\n2n + 1· 2n− 2\n2n− 1· ··· ·4\n5· 2\n3I0\nFinalement\nI0 =\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)0dt =\n∫ 1\n0\n1dt = (1 − 0)· 1 = 1 .\nIn = 2n\n2n + 1· 2n− 2\n2n− 1· ··· ·4\n5· 2\n3.\n3. En d´ eduire\nn∑_{k=0} (−1)k\n2k + 1\n(nₖ\n)\n: D’apr` es le binome de Newton, nous pouvons ´ ecrire\n(1−t2)n =\nn∑_{k=0} (nₖ\n)\n(−1)kt2k.\n\nAinsi\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)ndt =\n∫ 1\n0\nn∑_{k=0} (nₖ\n)\n(−1)kt2kdt\n=\nn∑_{k=0} (nₖ\n)\n(−1)k\n∫ 1\n0\nt2kdt\n=\nn∑_{k=0} (nₖ\n)\n(−1)k\n[ t2k+1\n2k + 1\n]1\n0\n=\nn∑_{k=0} (nₖ\n)\n(−1)k 1\n2k + 1.\nn∑_{k=0} (nₖ\n)\n(−1)k 1\n2k + 1 =\n∫ 1\n0\n(1−t2)ndt\n= In\n= 2n\n2n + 1· 2n− 2\n2n− 1· ··· ·4\n5· 2\n3."
