"section": "Exercice 1",
"label": "TD5 — corrigé · 2024-2025 — Exercice 1",
"text": "![exercice 1](https://data.cy.deltahmed.fr/DATA/TD5-Recursivite_Informatique2p1s2/exo1.jpg){: .w-75 .shadow .rounded-10 }\n\n\n1. On crée la version itérative du programme\n \n\n```c \nint powerIt(int a, int b) {\n    int result = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < b; i++) {\n        result *= a;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\n``` \n\n\n2. On crée maintenant la version récursive du programme\n \n\n```c \nint powerRec(int a, int b) {\n    if (b == 0) {\n        return 1;\n    }\n    return a * powerRec(a, b - 1);\n}\n\n``` \n\n\n3. On dessine l'arbre de récursion de la fonction\n \n\n```mermaid\nflowchart\n    n1([\"powerRec(3,4)\"])\n\tn1 --- n2([\"3 * powerRec(3,3)\"])\n\tn2 --- n3([\"3 * powerRec(3,2)\"])\n\tn3 --- n4([\"3 * powerRec(3,1)\"])\n\tn4 --- n5([\"3 * powerRec(3,0)\"])\n\tn7([\"3*3*3*3*1\"])\n\tn7 --- n8[\"3*3*3*1\"]\n\tn8 --- n9[\"3*3*1\"]\n\tn9 --- n10[\"3*1\"]\n\tn10 --- n11[\"1\"]\n\t\n``` \n\n<div id=\"2\"></div>"
},
