"text": "Exercice 5\n2. Si on utilise les coordon´ ees polaires :\n{ x = r cosθ\ny = r sinθ =⇒\n⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐\n∂x\n∂r\n∂x\n∂θ\n∂y\n∂r\n∂y\n∂θ\n⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐\n=\n⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐\ncosθ −r sinθ\nsinθ r cosθ\n⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐⏐\n= r,\nl’´ equation du disque donne :\n(r cos(θ)− 1)2 + (r sin(θ))2≤ 1 =⇒ r 2− 2r cos(θ)≤ 0\n=⇒ 0≤ r≤ 2 cos(θ).\nAinsi\n0≤ r≤ 2 cos(θ) et θ∈\n[\n−π\n2,π²\n]\n, imperatif pour avoir cos( θ)≥ 0.\nD’o` u\n∫ ∫\nD\n√\nx 2 + y 2dxdy =\n∫ π²\n− π²\n∫ 2 cos(θ)\n0\n√\nr 2 rdrdθ\n=\n∫ π²\n− π²\n∫ 2 cos(θ)\n0\nr 2 drdθ\n=\n∫ π²\n− π²\n8 cos3θ\n3 dθ."
